 "productionNotes": "Total: 1,270, and the sources agree on it. Wikipedia, evo, PistonHeads, Stuttcars, Hagerty, classic.com and an RM Sotheby's catalog essay on the 949th car all state 1,270, and Porsche's own May 2006 end-of-production release says more than 1,270 had been sold. A single outlier, Jalopnik, says Porsche reportedly built around 1,300; it is not used. The planned run was 1,500, per the March 2004 news item and evo, and PistonHeads recalls talk of 1,000 before that. The last car was built at Leipzig on Saturday, May 6, 2006. Where the sources split is the US share. Porsche's release counted 604 cars in North America at the end of the run; Wikipedia says 644 in the United States and 31 in Canada; Stuttcars says about 644 delivered to the US; Hagerty says roughly half of 1,270. None gives a model-year breakdown. The start year is also unsettled: Wikipedia and Porsche's 2025 newsroom release say 2003 to 2006, classic.com says 2004 to 2007, and US sales are documented from 2004. No source consulted breaks US cars out by model year, so this page does not split 2004, 2005 and 2006. NHTSA's recall covers the 2004 and 2005 build, which says something about the cars on the road but not about the count. No marque registry or club source was fetched for this page, so no chassis-level count exists here.",
